      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] My apologies for the previous hallucination regarding `fingerprint_auth_enabled()`. Since you were completely correct that it relies on `FP_CONTEXT_STATUS_SESSION_ESTABLISHED`, this new test actually needs that flag to be set in order to exercise the new code path!\n\nRight now, because `FP_CONTEXT_STATUS_SESSION_ESTABLISHED` is not set here, `fingerprint_auth_enabled()` returns false. This completely bypasses the new `if` block, making the test pass trivially by falling through to the end of the function.\n\nWe need to add the session established flag so it tests the `if (std::ranges::equal(...))` branch. \n\n```cpp\n\t/* Simulate an active session so fingerprint_auth_enabled() is true. */\n\tglobal_context.fp_encryption_status |\u003d\n\t\tFP_CONTEXT_STATUS_SESSION_ESTABLISHED;\n\n\t/*\n\t * Verify that executing FP_CONTEXT_GET_RESULT with the SAME\n\t * user ID succeeds (idempotent retry) even when fingerprint auth is active,\n\t * ensuring AP IPC timeouts do not break the state machine.\n\t */\n\tzassert_equal(EC_RES_SUCCESS,\n\t\t      ec_cmd_fp_context_v1(NULL, \u0026fp_context_params),\n\t\t      \"Idempotent context retries should be allowed\");\n\n\t/* Clean up */\n\tglobal_context.fp_encryption_status \u0026\u003d\n\t\t~FP_CONTEXT_STATUS_SESSION_ESTABLISHED;\n```\n*(Also, note the removal of the term \"FingerGuard\" from the comment to match the other changes!)*",
